  <revision rev="6" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>908e141848bb2417ff70b1dbfb75a489</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4019</version>
    <time>1793020643</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- updated to 0.4019
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-Starman/Changes
  0.4019  2026-10-24 02:02:21 PDT
          [SECURITY]
          - Stream chunked request bodies to the temporary buffer instead of
            holding whole chunks in memory (CVE-2026-115824) bsc#1287697
          - Parse chunk-size lines in linear time with a 4 KiB length limit and
            strict syntax; malformed lines get 400 (CVE-2026-115822) bsc#1287695
          - Do not send a response body for HEAD requests or 1xx, 204 and 304
            responses, on both the array and streaming paths (CVE-2026-115823) bsc#1287696
          - Limit how long a request body may take to arrive: --read-timeout
            (default 5 seconds) now also applies to each wait for more of the
            body, and the new --body-timeout option limits the total time
            (default 300 seconds; raise it or set it to 0 for slower uploads).
            Expiry gets 408 (CVE-2026-115817) bsc#1287694
          - Reject Transfer-Encoding other than &quot;chunked&quot; (400/501) and close
            the connection after a request with both Transfer-Encoding and
            Content-Length. Completes the fix for CVE-2026-40560 bsc#1263364
          - Reject malformed, negative and conflicting Content-Length headers
            with 400
          - Reject malformed header field names: whitespace before the colon,
            obs-fold, and Content-Length/Transfer-Encoding spelled with &quot;_&quot;
          - Read request bodies with exact framing: keep the bytes after a body
            for the next pipelined request, consume chunked trailers (up to
            16 KiB), and reject bodies cut short by EOF with 400 instead of
            dispatching a partial body
          - Parse each request header exactly once and skip empty lines before
            the request line (a request could be dispatched twice with the
            pure-Perl HTTP::Parser::XS backend)
          - Respond with 500 instead of dispatching a truncated body when the</comment>
    <requestid>1392696</requestid>
  </revision>
